1
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:46,533
[Island of Affection – A new moon rises.]

2
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:51,633
Welcome to the Island of Affection.

3
00:00:51,633 --> 00:00:53,633
Your journey of love begins now.

4
00:00:53,633 --> 00:00:56,100
[Yellow VS Red]
The Arena of Affection is about to open.

5
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:58,900
The final winner gets the right

6
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:00,066
[Score Board Yellow VS Red]
to ask someone out.

7
00:01:00,066 --> 00:01:02,766
I haven't had a chance to talk
to the person I'm interested in.

8
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,900
I need that dating chance.

9
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:07,200
If there's no chance,
you have to create one.

10
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:09,266
If I like someone,
I'll take the initiative.

11
00:01:09,266 --> 00:01:11,300
[At first sight,
we're just a shy crescent on the horizon.]

12
00:01:12,133 --> 00:01:13,133
Hello.

13
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:14,366
Hello.

14
00:01:15,066 --> 00:01:16,166
Hello.

15
00:01:23,133 --> 00:01:24,433
Invite the girl you're interested in.

16
00:01:24,466 --> 00:01:26,300
You go. I'm kinda shy.

17
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:27,500
What's wrong with them?

18
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,966
Why does no guy take the lead?

19
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,800
"The ones who can't
get into a relationship."

20
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,500
[Every story begins
with a moment too timid to speak.]

21
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,633
Who is this?

22
00:01:35,066 --> 00:01:36,166
- Hello.
- Hello.

23
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:39,066
Far away, I saw a lonely figure
sitting here.

24
00:01:40,133 --> 00:01:41,433
So happy.

25
00:01:41,466 --> 00:01:43,800
We are like two bachelors
with nowhere to go.

26
00:01:43,833 --> 00:01:45,866
She's dating someone else.
What would you…?

27
00:01:45,866 --> 00:01:47,700
Then I might need to make a move.

28
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:49,933
Do you believe
in love at first sight or…?

29
00:01:49,933 --> 00:01:50,466
Love at first sight.

30
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:51,533
It has to be.

31
00:01:51,533 --> 00:01:53,000
[If your feel it, be the first butterfly
to fly into the wind.]

32
00:01:53,033 --> 00:01:53,833
He approached you on day one.

33
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:55,700
That takes a lot of courage.

34
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:57,000
Maybe it's not full-on affection.

35
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:59,466
But at least he feels
something special for you.

36
00:01:59,466 --> 00:02:00,500
I followed my heart.

37
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,033
I gave an extra vote to the guy
I felt a connection with.

38
00:02:03,066 --> 00:02:05,466
Vinson. I think he's been
giving me signals.

39
00:02:06,866 --> 00:02:07,600
Pinky promise.

40
00:02:07,633 --> 00:02:09,366
We're doing this? OK.

41
00:02:10,033 --> 00:02:13,266
[The sun rises and sets.]

42
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:16,966
[Can a new dawn trade itself
for moonlight leading to you?]

43
00:02:32,833 --> 00:02:37,366
[Love Wins All]

44
00:02:38,266 --> 00:02:39,800
We're all kind of

45
00:02:39,833 --> 00:02:41,500
worried that

46
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:43,133
we'll have to leave.

47
00:02:43,133 --> 00:02:44,833
We can't avoid it.

48
00:02:44,866 --> 00:02:47,333
But I hope I can stay at least today.

49
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:49,600
I've thought about leaving today.

50
00:02:49,633 --> 00:02:51,066
There is no script at all.

51
00:02:51,066 --> 00:02:53,533
I have no idea what will happen.

52
00:02:57,033 --> 00:02:58,900
Dear islanders,

53
00:02:59,866 --> 00:03:02,000
after a day together,

54
00:03:02,033 --> 00:03:04,466
you can all stay for now.

55
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,300
[Day 2 - Everyone's safe.]

56
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:08,300
Big baby.

57
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:09,400
Actually, the more, the merrier.

58
00:03:09,433 --> 00:03:10,466
Yeah.

59
00:03:10,466 --> 00:03:11,600
What are you reading?

60
00:03:11,633 --> 00:03:12,566
Chinese medicine.

61
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,233
It's packed with wisdom.

62
00:03:14,233 --> 00:03:15,466
He fell asleep

63
00:03:15,466 --> 00:03:16,500
and smacked his lips.

64
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:18,333
Everyone heard it.

65
00:03:18,333 --> 00:03:19,133
Really?

66
00:03:19,133 --> 00:03:21,366
We're making coffee.

67
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,033
But please note…

68
00:03:24,233 --> 00:03:25,633
But please note

69
00:03:25,633 --> 00:03:27,133
that in 24 hours,

70
00:03:27,133 --> 00:03:29,033
someone will have to leave.

71
00:03:30,066 --> 00:03:31,733
[24 hours later,]
The departure countdown has begun.

72
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:33,400
[someone will leave the island.]
The departure countdown has begun.

73
00:03:33,433 --> 00:03:35,066
Someone will leave tomorrow morning.

74
00:03:35,066 --> 00:03:36,366
I immediately felt

75
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,533
the pressure.

76
00:03:37,533 --> 00:03:38,966
At first,
I thought, "Just go with the flow."

77
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,900
But now I feel like I want to stay
a few more days.

78
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:41,800
Yeah.

79
00:03:41,833 --> 00:03:42,700
When I heard

80
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:43,933
someone would leave
in only 24 hours,

81
00:03:43,933 --> 00:03:44,400
I think

82
00:03:44,433 --> 00:03:46,900
we need to be more proactive.

83
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:47,500
[EP02 – Don't wait. Make the first move.]

84
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:51,033
[Today's Affection Moon Phase: Crescent]

85
00:03:54,733 --> 00:03:56,433
If this were real life,

86
00:03:56,466 --> 00:03:58,266
would you make the first move?

87
00:03:58,266 --> 00:04:00,100
[Would you make the first move in love?]
He'd have to give me a signal first

88
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:01,800
[Would you make the first move in love?]
or say something. Then I'd act.

89
00:04:01,833 --> 00:04:03,700
Yeah, me too.

90
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:04,366
If a guy

91
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,333
likes you even a little,

92
00:04:05,333 --> 00:04:06,466
he should make the first move.

93
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:08,133
Then I can respond.

94
00:04:08,133 --> 00:04:10,033
We gotta act first.

95
00:04:10,066 --> 00:04:11,666
You know, last night,

96
00:04:11,666 --> 00:04:12,933
I was chatting with one of the girls.

97
00:04:12,933 --> 00:04:15,200
She said we boys were way too passive.

98
00:04:15,233 --> 00:04:16,133
Who are you looking for?

99
00:04:16,133 --> 00:04:16,800
It doesn't matter.

100
00:04:16,833 --> 00:04:18,500
Just walk around

101
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:19,833
[From being chosen to choosing]
and talk to them.

102
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:21,300
[Knocking First]

103
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,933
Ma, who are you looking for?

104
00:04:22,933 --> 00:04:24,433
Autumn.

105
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:25,933
I'm sure that I have an interest

106
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:27,466
in someone now.

107
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:28,566
What?

108
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,533
I didn't hear it. What?

109
00:04:30,533 --> 00:04:31,033
She said

110
00:04:31,066 --> 00:04:32,533
she's interested in someone.

111
00:04:32,866 --> 00:04:33,733
You each get one chance,

112
00:04:33,733 --> 00:04:35,433
and I'll admit it if you're right.

113
00:04:37,866 --> 00:04:38,966
Just one chance.

114
00:04:43,633 --> 00:04:44,300
You're good.

115
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:45,400
Am I right?

116
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:45,933
You're good.

117
00:04:48,933 --> 00:04:52,166
You'll work together

118
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,333
to make your own lunch today.

119
00:04:53,333 --> 00:04:54,633
I want to cook with him.

120
00:04:54,666 --> 00:04:55,966
[Can't Wait]
Go on, hurry now.

121
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,066
I want to get closer to him.

122
00:04:59,066 --> 00:05:00,166
Babe!

123
00:05:01,266 --> 00:05:02,900
I gotta learn from you.

124
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:04,166
[Model of Initiative]

125
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,400
Whatever.

126
00:05:05,433 --> 00:05:06,433
I like him.

127
00:05:11,266 --> 00:05:12,066
[Islanders make lunch together]
Let's divvy up the ingredients.

128
00:05:12,066 --> 00:05:12,733
[for the first time.]
Let's divvy up the ingredients.

129
00:05:12,733 --> 00:05:14,066
Two people peel the garlic.

130
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:15,133
OK, guys?

131
00:05:15,433 --> 00:05:16,666
Let's make spicy and sour
shredded potatoes.

132
00:05:19,233 --> 00:05:20,300
Who is the chef?

133
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:20,900
Tutu (Wang Meng).

134
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:21,733
[Chef]

135
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:23,333
I love cooking.

136
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:24,400
I feel happy and fulfilled

137
00:05:24,433 --> 00:05:25,833
when I cook for people

138
00:05:25,833 --> 00:05:27,700
and they love the food.

139
00:05:28,333 --> 00:05:29,366
Come on.

140
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,233
Start cutting.

141
00:05:42,266 --> 00:05:44,300
[Moving Closer to the Sink]

142
00:05:45,066 --> 00:05:46,066
They've started.

143
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:49,400
[Target Boy?]

144
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:53,700
[Hinting]

145
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,133
[Approaching]

146
00:05:59,266 --> 00:06:00,266
I can help you wash it.

147
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,066
No, don't wash it.

148
00:06:02,066 --> 00:06:03,800
Just break it into florets and blanch.

149
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,266
You sound professional.

150
00:06:06,266 --> 00:06:07,100
Impressive.

151
00:06:07,133 --> 00:06:09,400
[An Unexpected Compliment]

152
00:06:10,866 --> 00:06:13,200
[To feel is instinct; to act is a choice.]

153
00:06:13,733 --> 00:06:14,333
Tutu (Wang Meng).

154
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:14,933
You're good.

155
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,900
I want to cook with him.

156
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:19,200
Go on, hurry now.

157
00:06:19,233 --> 00:06:20,300
I want to get closer to him.

158
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:22,866
Whatever.

159
00:06:22,866 --> 00:06:23,866
I like him.

160
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:26,933
You're making me blush.

161
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:32,966
It's falling apart.

162
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,233
Stop washing it. It'll get mushy.

163
00:06:36,933 --> 00:06:38,233
I think if I keep looking at you,

164
00:06:38,266 --> 00:06:40,533
the footage will feel full of love.

165
00:06:40,533 --> 00:06:41,266
What?

166
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:41,700
I said we…

167
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:42,300
Look to your left.

168
00:06:53,633 --> 00:06:54,733
Good spot you got there.

169
00:06:56,633 --> 00:06:58,500
[Can't Help Smiling]

170
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,700
I think boys and girls
can all take the initiative.

171
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:03,000
When there's a window,

172
00:07:03,033 --> 00:07:04,133
or you just have a feeling,

173
00:07:04,133 --> 00:07:04,733
whoever dares to act first

174
00:07:04,733 --> 00:07:06,800
gets to enjoy love first.

175
00:07:08,266 --> 00:07:10,066
I can give you a hand.

176
00:07:10,066 --> 00:07:11,500
Can you pull some tissues for me?

177
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:11,966
OK.

178
00:07:12,633 --> 00:07:14,333
[Heart Racing Beneath the Calm.]

179
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:17,600
Can this do?

180
00:07:17,633 --> 00:07:18,866
Sure.

181
00:07:18,866 --> 00:07:19,366
I'm sweating.

182
00:07:21,533 --> 00:07:22,733
When your dish is done,

183
00:07:22,733 --> 00:07:24,266
can we say that we made it together?

184
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:26,900
[Waiting for a Response]

185
00:07:27,666 --> 00:07:28,600
OK.

186
00:07:28,633 --> 00:07:29,900
We can.

187
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,633
I usually only eat one meal a day,

188
00:07:32,666 --> 00:07:34,000
but I can eat two meals today.

189
00:07:34,033 --> 00:07:36,466
It's too hot in here.

190
00:07:36,466 --> 00:07:37,666
It's so hot in this room.

191
00:07:37,666 --> 00:07:38,700
I'll fan you a bit.

192
00:07:40,633 --> 00:07:41,766
I feel

193
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,433
[Chop, Chop, Chop]
it gets very hot at noon.

194
00:07:51,066 --> 00:07:52,266
I think there is something going on

195
00:07:52,266 --> 00:07:53,533
between the two of us.

196
00:07:53,533 --> 00:07:55,366
I don't want to miss this chance.

197
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:56,533
When there's a chance,

198
00:07:56,533 --> 00:07:58,066
and I don't grasp it,

199
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:00,366
the outcome may be different.

200
00:08:01,266 --> 00:08:03,600
When we were cooking in the kitchen,

201
00:08:03,633 --> 00:08:04,900
Xue paid the most attention to me.

202
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:06,133
She was quite proactive.

203
00:08:06,133 --> 00:08:07,933
Don't stuff yourselves

204
00:08:07,933 --> 00:08:08,600
before lunchtime.

205
00:08:10,866 --> 00:08:12,733
So? Have you tried their dishes?

206
00:08:12,733 --> 00:08:13,166
No.

207
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:15,066
I want to eat shredded potatoes first.

208
00:08:15,066 --> 00:08:16,100
OK.

209
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:17,600
It's my favorite dish.

210
00:08:17,633 --> 00:08:18,866
I'll wait for this one.

211
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:29,066
Which of these guys

212
00:08:29,066 --> 00:08:30,866
impressed you the most?

213
00:08:30,866 --> 00:08:32,533
I think it's you.

214
00:08:32,666 --> 00:08:35,800
[I think it's you.]

215
00:08:37,466 --> 00:08:38,666
I'm not dead yet.

216
00:08:38,666 --> 00:08:39,766
I was standing right there.

217
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:41,800
[Well, that's awkward.]

218
00:08:42,233 --> 00:08:44,100
At first, everyone gathered
around Tutu (Wang Meng).

219
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:45,966
He was cutting the vegetables,
looking cute.

220
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,933
[And I saw Xiyao following him around.]

221
00:08:49,066 --> 00:08:49,533
[Outsider]

222
00:08:49,533 --> 00:08:51,066
[Outsider]
I didn't understand at first,

223
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:52,366
[Outsider]
so I was just standing there.

224
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:53,733
And I couldn't help much.

225
00:08:53,733 --> 00:08:55,033
I just tried to get busy.

226
00:08:55,066 --> 00:08:57,266
I washed some vegetables,
turned around, and saw

227
00:08:58,033 --> 00:08:59,533
Xiyao was still standing
next to Tutu (Wang Meng).

228
00:08:59,533 --> 00:09:00,233
She didn't do anything.

229
00:09:00,266 --> 00:09:01,566
Just keeping him company.

230
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,866
I was like, "So you're just gonna
be with Tutu today?"

231
00:09:03,866 --> 00:09:04,966
I was planning

232
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,100
to talk to her a bit more.

233
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:08,166
But she didn't give me the chance.

234
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,500
She chose Tutu (Wang Meng).

235
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:10,433
So I figured

236
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:11,333
I should just back off.

237
00:09:16,733 --> 00:09:18,466
He's a chef.

238
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:20,033
I can see that.

239
00:09:20,066 --> 00:09:21,000
Yeah.

240
00:09:21,033 --> 00:09:22,100
He's making it so mysterious.

241
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:23,000
No,

242
00:09:23,033 --> 00:09:24,166
I'm 100% sure

243
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:25,600
that my profession is not a chef.

244
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:28,400
Did you two just know each other?

245
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:28,733
[Curious]
Who?

246
00:09:28,733 --> 00:09:29,733
[Curious]
You two.

247
00:09:29,733 --> 00:09:30,933
We actually go way back.

248
00:09:30,933 --> 00:09:31,800
I don't buy it.

249
00:09:31,833 --> 00:09:32,933
[Start a Conversation]

250
00:09:33,066 --> 00:09:33,800
It's true.

251
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:36,966
Then what's his name?

252
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,433
The name he uses in this show.

253
00:09:39,433 --> 00:09:40,766
What is it?

254
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:41,700
Wang Meng.

255
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:44,933
I think he (Ma Haoxiang) is

256
00:09:44,933 --> 00:09:46,666
my type,

257
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:48,400
but we actually don't
have a lot of contact.

258
00:09:48,433 --> 00:09:50,466
So I tried to interact with him more.

259
00:09:50,633 --> 00:09:52,866
Drizzle some oil on top.

260
00:09:52,866 --> 00:09:54,600
You know how?

261
00:09:54,633 --> 00:09:55,533
[Following]
I do.

262
00:09:55,533 --> 00:09:56,533
[Following]
I know how to do it.

263
00:09:56,533 --> 00:09:57,666
It's here.

264
00:09:57,700 --> 00:09:58,400
[Oil is here.]
Wait.

265
00:09:58,833 --> 00:10:00,866
I thought you meant to heat it up
before drizzling it.

266
00:10:00,866 --> 00:10:01,933
No.

267
00:10:01,933 --> 00:10:02,733
Can you do it?

268
00:10:02,733 --> 00:10:04,000
Well, I can't.

269
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:11,033
What are you doing?

270
00:10:11,033 --> 00:10:13,333
I'm blanching broccoli.

271
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:14,233
OK, thank you.

272
00:10:23,233 --> 00:10:24,266
What are you making?

273
00:10:24,266 --> 00:10:24,900
[Proactive]
This.

274
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:26,300
[Proactive]
I'm just here to assist.

275
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:27,033
A professional assistant.

276
00:10:27,066 --> 00:10:28,200
Really?

277
00:10:29,133 --> 00:10:29,966
Pan (Pan Xiaoyi),

278
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,800
did anyone tell you that you looked like

279
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:34,066
Bai Jingting?

280
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,866
I'm a fan of Bai Jingting
and Wang Sulong.

281
00:10:36,866 --> 00:10:38,100
Is this

282
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:39,566
choy sum or something else?

283
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,666
Why does it look different from usual?

284
00:10:41,666 --> 00:10:42,600
I don't know the name.

285
00:10:42,633 --> 00:10:43,700
Maybe it's Shanghai bok choy.

286
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:45,233
It's so long.

287
00:10:45,266 --> 00:10:48,333
I pulled all the stalks.

288
00:10:48,333 --> 00:10:49,433
OK.

289
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:57,633
Just call me Xiaxia (Xia Boyan).

290
00:10:58,866 --> 00:10:59,866
I'll bet on you.

291
00:10:59,866 --> 00:11:00,766
Then, I'll bet on you, too.

292
00:11:04,333 --> 00:11:05,166
What's wrong?

293
00:11:06,466 --> 00:11:07,133
I'm 'unemployed',

294
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:09,333
just wandering around.

295
00:11:23,133 --> 00:11:23,666
[Met on Day One]
Hello.

296
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:24,333
[Met on Day One]
Hello.

297
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:25,533
Hello.

298
00:11:25,533 --> 00:11:26,000
Hello.

299
00:11:26,033 --> 00:11:27,366
Pan (Pan Xiaoyi).

300
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:28,200
Huihui (Duan Danhui).

301
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:29,500
When I was selecting the quadrant,

302
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:31,766
I met Pan (Pan Xiaoyi),

303
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:33,233
and my heart

304
00:11:33,233 --> 00:11:34,133
was beating so fast.

305
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:41,133
[At a Loss]

306
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:48,000
[Keep Smiling]

307
00:11:48,533 --> 00:11:49,733
I don't know how to cook.

308
00:11:49,733 --> 00:11:51,333
I can only stand by the AC.

309
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:53,833
What should I do?

310
00:11:53,866 --> 00:11:55,666
[Conflicted]

311
00:11:55,833 --> 00:11:58,733
[Eyes confess a thousand times,
but how to speak first?]

312
00:11:59,333 --> 00:12:00,866
[Show Up]

313
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:03,100
[Closing in Again]

314
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:05,033
[Closing in Again]
What is it that makes you so happy?

315
00:12:05,333 --> 00:12:06,600
Nothing.

316
00:12:06,633 --> 00:12:07,666
You're a happy person.

317
00:12:07,666 --> 00:12:10,000
I just look full of energy every day.

318
00:12:11,333 --> 00:12:12,966
[Peeking]

319
00:12:15,833 --> 00:12:18,900
[Make a Move or Just Wait?]

320
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:26,333
[Walk Away Again]

321
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,700
Someone help me!

322
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:31,366
[Conflicted]
He's quiet

323
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:34,100
and refined

324
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:34,900
in the crowd,

325
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:37,133
which makes me feel he's the type

326
00:12:37,133 --> 00:12:39,133
who needs the other person

327
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:40,466
to take the first step toward him.

328
00:12:42,033 --> 00:12:44,433
[Third Attempt to Get Closer]

329
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:51,100
[Sneaking Around]

330
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,366
[Turn Away]

331
00:12:52,733 --> 00:12:54,366
I'm like a thief.

332
00:13:01,533 --> 00:13:02,933
What are you doing?

333
00:13:02,933 --> 00:13:04,333
[Finally Taking That First Step]
Looking for something to do.

334
00:13:04,333 --> 00:13:05,533
Gotta move quickly.

335
00:13:06,633 --> 00:13:08,166
Did you peel these?

336
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:10,266
I peeled these.

337
00:13:10,266 --> 00:13:11,466
So your hands smell now.

338
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,300
It's OK.

339
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:38,466
Good, you can still shake hands.

340
00:13:38,466 --> 00:13:38,866
Now your hands smell, too.

341
00:13:40,133 --> 00:13:41,066
Oh, yeah, they do!

342
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,266
I'm lying.

343
00:13:43,266 --> 00:13:44,000
Can you crack eggs?

344
00:13:44,033 --> 00:13:45,766
I can't even do that.

345
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:46,266
Crack eggs?

346
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:51,166
[Blurt it out already.]

347
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:52,200
[Blurt it out already.]
I don't cook much either.

348
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:53,300
I cook for my little brother sometimes,

349
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:53,966
but he's…

350
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:54,600
You have a brother?

351
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:56,500
I have one, too.

352
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:59,200
Younger brothers usually
fear their sisters,

353
00:13:59,233 --> 00:13:59,833
right?

354
00:13:59,833 --> 00:14:01,166
My brother is like that.

355
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:02,333
How about yours?

356
00:14:02,833 --> 00:14:04,166
He doesn't dare say anything

357
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:06,100
because I'm the 'bad cop' in my family.

358
00:14:07,833 --> 00:14:09,666
Do you have a good temper?

359
00:14:09,666 --> 00:14:10,733
What do you think?

360
00:14:10,733 --> 00:14:12,666
What's your first impression of me?

361
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:14,766
But when we first met,
we were like this…

362
00:14:16,433 --> 00:14:17,533
You remember it well.

363
00:14:23,266 --> 00:14:24,366
What are you gonna make?

364
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:25,700
Sweet and Sour Spareribs.

365
00:14:26,733 --> 00:14:28,333
I like it very much.

366
00:14:28,333 --> 00:14:29,366
Are these Cola Chicken Wings?

367
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:29,800
Yes.

368
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:30,800
Before I came here, they asked me,

369
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,400
"What dishes a guy cooks
will impress you?"

370
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:33,600
I said Cola Chicken Wings.

371
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:34,633
Why didn't you show off your skills?

372
00:14:34,633 --> 00:14:36,066
All the chefs are here today.

373
00:14:36,066 --> 00:14:39,700
I don't want to show off
in front of the pros.

374
00:14:43,233 --> 00:14:44,266
Thank you.

375
00:14:44,266 --> 00:14:45,600
I have to wait a bit longer.

376
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,200
I'll wait with you.

377
00:14:48,533 --> 00:14:50,133
[Sweet Punch]

378
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:52,333
What?

379
00:14:59,133 --> 00:15:00,633
[Ma Haoxiang: Lunchtime!]

380
00:15:01,633 --> 00:15:02,366
These seats are taken.

381
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:04,833
It's crowded next to you.

382
00:15:05,900 --> 00:15:07,166
[Staring]

383
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:07,933
[Target Seat]
Is this seat taken?

384
00:15:07,933 --> 00:15:08,566
[Target Seat]

385
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:09,266
[Target Seat Seat Taken]
Sun Shuo.

386
00:15:09,266 --> 00:15:09,700
[Seat Taken]

387
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:10,233
[Seat Taken]
Shuo…

388
00:15:10,266 --> 00:15:11,533
[Have to Give Up]

389
00:15:11,533 --> 00:15:11,733
It's OK. Just sit here.

390
00:15:11,733 --> 00:15:12,833
There's a seat here.

391
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:14,666
Let me sit for a while.

392
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:22,733
You wanna try
this creative zucchini dish?

393
00:15:30,333 --> 00:15:31,233
Dropped a piece.

394
00:15:31,533 --> 00:15:32,133
Here.

395
00:15:32,133 --> 00:15:32,866
I tried it, babe.

396
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:33,600
Already?

397
00:15:36,933 --> 00:15:39,366
This one has shrimp paste.

398
00:15:39,733 --> 00:15:40,266
Thanks.

399
00:15:43,333 --> 00:15:44,400
Try it.

400
00:15:44,433 --> 00:15:45,933
A creative dish made by Autumn.

401
00:15:48,333 --> 00:15:49,433
Delicious.

402
00:15:54,466 --> 00:15:56,900
[Lost in Thought]

403
00:16:00,666 --> 00:16:01,800
Say it.

404
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:04,466
You first or me?

405
00:16:04,466 --> 00:16:05,566
You go first.

406
00:16:08,033 --> 00:16:09,166
So nervous.

407
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:10,233
[Curious +1]

408
00:16:10,233 --> 00:16:11,166
[Curious +1 Curious +2]

409
00:16:15,433 --> 00:16:16,900
Guys, I have something to say.

410
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:18,000
Yeah, me too.

411
00:16:18,033 --> 00:16:18,633
Yeah.

412
00:16:20,933 --> 00:16:21,266
[Ready for the Tea]

413
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:22,700
[Ready for the Tea]
Are you announcing something?

414
00:16:23,233 --> 00:16:25,233
Why so serious?

415
00:16:25,233 --> 00:16:26,533
Stand together.

416
00:16:26,533 --> 00:16:27,533
Tell us.

417
00:16:27,866 --> 00:16:29,800
There is something serious

418
00:16:29,833 --> 00:16:31,533
we want to let everyone know.

419
00:16:31,533 --> 00:16:33,833
We want to apologize for that.

420
00:16:39,066 --> 00:16:42,333
We made a decision yesterday,

421
00:16:42,333 --> 00:16:44,566
but it was very wrong.

422
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:46,600
We deeply regretted it,

423
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,333
and it also affected you guys.

424
00:16:48,333 --> 00:16:49,766
Last night,

425
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,600
when we were voting with Moonstones,

426
00:16:52,733 --> 00:16:54,133
because yesterday I felt

427
00:16:54,133 --> 00:16:55,833
I was a lot like an NPC,

428
00:16:55,866 --> 00:16:57,133
and I was joking around

429
00:16:57,133 --> 00:16:58,400
most of the time,

430
00:16:58,433 --> 00:16:59,533
and he…

431
00:16:59,533 --> 00:17:00,166
The thing is,

432
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:02,133
we worried that

433
00:17:02,133 --> 00:17:03,233
nobody would give

434
00:17:03,266 --> 00:17:04,933
their Moonstones to us,

435
00:17:04,933 --> 00:17:06,033
so we both voted for each other.

436
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:15,633
[Last Night Before the Vote]
It's OK, we can…

437
00:17:15,633 --> 00:17:16,433
[Last Night Before the Vote]
There are lots of people.

438
00:17:16,433 --> 00:17:17,700
[Last Night Before the Vote]
Let's take a look.

439
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:18,633
[Kong Xichen: Autumn wants to see you.]
Autumn wants to see you.

440
00:17:18,666 --> 00:17:19,166
[Ma Haoxiang: Really? Kong Xichen: Hm!]
Really?

441
00:17:20,266 --> 00:17:20,800
Is it a date?

442
00:17:21,833 --> 00:17:22,466
What's up?

443
00:17:22,466 --> 00:17:23,566
[Ma Going to Autumn.]

444
00:17:23,600 --> 00:17:24,133
[Ma Going to Autumn.]
Autumn.

445
00:17:25,033 --> 00:17:25,966
Come, I wanna discuss something.

446
00:17:26,733 --> 00:17:27,533
Have you decided

447
00:17:27,533 --> 00:17:28,800
who you want to vote for later?

448
00:17:28,833 --> 00:17:29,900
I can vote for you.

449
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:31,533
That'll be great. You know what?

450
00:17:31,533 --> 00:17:33,666
I don't want to leave the island.

451
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:35,133
[Autumn doesn't want to leave.]
Not so soon.

452
00:17:35,133 --> 00:17:35,866
[Autumn doesn't want to leave.]
But you know,

453
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:37,133
[Autumn doesn't want to leave.]
the 'funny girl' never gets the romance.

454
00:17:37,133 --> 00:17:39,133
Nobody votes for the 'funny girl'.

455
00:17:39,133 --> 00:17:40,300
[Autumn worries]
If no one votes for you,

456
00:17:40,333 --> 00:17:40,966
[no one will vote for her.]
you're gonna leave?

457
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:41,733
Yes.

458
00:17:41,733 --> 00:17:42,666
Let's vote for each other.

459
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:43,333
[Promise to vote for each other.]
OK.

460
00:17:43,333 --> 00:17:44,200
[Promise to vote for each other.]
Then, it's settled.

461
00:17:44,233 --> 00:17:45,066
[Promise to vote for each other.]
You vote for me.

462
00:17:45,066 --> 00:17:45,566
[Promise to vote for each other.]
I vote for you.

463
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:46,233
[Promise to vote for each other.]
Good, pinky promise.

464
00:17:46,233 --> 00:17:46,966
[Promise to vote for each other.]
You vote for me.

465
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:47,733
[Promise to vote for each other.]
Yeah.

466
00:17:49,133 --> 00:17:50,733
It's a date, you know?

467
00:17:50,733 --> 00:17:52,866
Laugh out loud.

468
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:53,966
I'll give all five

469
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,100
to him.

470
00:17:56,733 --> 00:17:57,400
[Autumn gives Ma Haoxiang 5 Moonstones.]
[Ma Haoxiang gives Autumn 5 Moonstones.]

471
00:17:57,433 --> 00:17:58,066
Let's go.

472
00:18:00,433 --> 00:18:00,766
[This Morning]

473
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,400
[This Morning]
Ma, who are you looking for?

474
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:03,733
[This Morning]
Autumn.

475
00:18:03,733 --> 00:18:04,333
[This Morning]
Come on.

476
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:06,533
Let's talk about it.

477
00:18:06,533 --> 00:18:07,333
Here's what I think.

478
00:18:08,533 --> 00:18:09,833
Look, the thing is

479
00:18:09,866 --> 00:18:12,933
this is, you know,

480
00:18:12,933 --> 00:18:13,733
the Island of Affection.

481
00:18:13,733 --> 00:18:15,433
Not the Island of Survival, right?

482
00:18:15,466 --> 00:18:16,866
I feel like

483
00:18:16,866 --> 00:18:17,700
[Realize they shouldn't just think
about staying on the island.]

484
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:19,733
we shouldn't think about things
just from the perspective

485
00:18:19,733 --> 00:18:21,566
of staying on the island.

486
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,533
Everyone else is being genuine,

487
00:18:22,533 --> 00:18:24,000
and if we do this,

488
00:18:24,033 --> 00:18:25,433
I feel like
it's not really respecting them.

489
00:18:25,433 --> 00:18:27,533
It's also not fair

490
00:18:27,533 --> 00:18:28,566
to the other guys

491
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:30,433
[Worry that
their action is unfair to others.]

492
00:18:30,433 --> 00:18:31,333
and girls.

493
00:18:31,333 --> 00:18:33,200
Because we were dishonest, right?

494
00:18:33,233 --> 00:18:35,066
I think we got it wrong.

495
00:18:35,066 --> 00:18:36,733
We thought of the Moonstone part

496
00:18:36,733 --> 00:18:38,166
as part

497
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:41,666
of the competition.

498
00:18:41,666 --> 00:18:43,300
Maybe we didn't figure out

499
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:45,400
the right way to approach it.

500
00:18:45,433 --> 00:18:46,166
Yeah.

501
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,000
I think

502
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
the decision we made yesterday

503
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:50,933
was a bit reckless.

504
00:18:50,933 --> 00:18:52,800
We didn't think it through. Right?

505
00:18:52,833 --> 00:18:54,733
Yeah.

506
00:18:54,733 --> 00:18:56,133
We should tell everyone

507
00:18:56,133 --> 00:18:57,333
at lunchtime.

508
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:09,400
So this is not fair.

509
00:19:09,433 --> 00:19:10,166
The more we think about it,

510
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:11,433
the more we feel sorry for you guys.

511
00:19:11,433 --> 00:19:12,033
Sorry, everyone.

512
00:19:12,033 --> 00:19:13,233
My sincere apology.

513
00:19:13,833 --> 00:19:14,966
It's OK.

514
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,200
It's alright.

515
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:18,333
Don't worry about it.

516
00:19:18,666 --> 00:19:19,666
It's OK.

517
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:22,866
To survive on the Island of Affection,

518
00:19:22,866 --> 00:19:24,166
we may all have pressures

519
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:26,000
and mixed feelings.

520
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,033
In a high-pressure environment,

521
00:19:28,033 --> 00:19:30,433
everyone will be troubled

522
00:19:30,433 --> 00:19:34,266
by problems about staying or leaving.

523
00:19:34,266 --> 00:19:35,300
Yeah, so…

524
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:37,000
I think it is normal
for these things to happen.

525
00:19:37,733 --> 00:19:39,566
I don't think it's a big deal.

526
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:42,833
There are competitions on this island.

527
00:19:42,833 --> 00:19:44,366
So I think it's normal

528
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:46,200
to figure out ways to stay.

529
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:48,066
Their apology was

530
00:19:48,066 --> 00:19:49,300
actually pretty sincere.

531
00:19:49,533 --> 00:19:49,866
It's OK.

532
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:52,366
If you two turn the fake act
into something real,

533
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,733
it'll be epic.

534
00:19:57,266 --> 00:19:59,133
So what should you two do?

535
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:01,200
All the Moonstones he gave me are void.

536
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:03,700
Whether the ones I gave you count,

537
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:05,600
you can think about it.

538
00:20:05,633 --> 00:20:06,366
I am so handsome,

539
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:07,133
someone must've voted for me.

540
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:10,700
Just kidding.

541
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:13,500
Anyway, we hope that's the case.

542
00:20:13,733 --> 00:20:14,366
Well,

543
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:15,866
we appreciate that

544
00:20:15,866 --> 00:20:17,566
you two came clean to us.

545
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:18,400
[Earn Everyone's Understanding]
Yes.

546
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:19,300
[Earn Everyone's Understanding]
I'm really sorry.

547
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:20,166
[Earn Everyone's Understanding]
Sorry.

548
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:23,166
We'd do anything for you to compensate.

549
00:20:24,066 --> 00:20:25,866
It's alright.

550
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:27,333
Regarding the votes

551
00:20:27,333 --> 00:20:30,833
for Ma Haoxiang and Autumn last night,

552
00:20:30,866 --> 00:20:32,000
other islanders

553
00:20:32,033 --> 00:20:35,066
can choose
to maintain last night's results

554
00:20:35,066 --> 00:20:36,600
and keep things as they are

555
00:20:36,633 --> 00:20:39,500
or give Ma Haoxiang and Autumn

556
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:41,500
